DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260820T200000
SUMMARY:Member Meet Up: Night Shift Brewery Esplanade
LOCATION:Offsite: Night Shift Brewery Esplanade
DESCRIPTION:Category: Member Mixer\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: unlimit
 ed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/197999\n\nJoin fell
 ow members for an early summer evening at Night Shift Brewery on the Espla
 nade\, a lively outdoor beer garden set along the Charles River.\n\nThis c
 asual gathering offers an easy setting to connect\, unwind\, and enjoy a c
 urated selection of beers\, hard seltzers\, wines\, and non-alcoholic opti
 ons. Whether catching up with familiar faces or meeting someone new\, the 
 atmosphere is designed to be social\, welcoming\, and effortlessly enjoyab
 le.\n\nDogs are welcome so feel free to bring your four-legged companion a
 long for the evening.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for mem
 bers only. Each member will receive two complimentary drinks\, followed by
  a cash bar. Food will be available for purchase.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/197999
CATEGORIES:Member Mixer
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-198805@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260822T100000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260822T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260822T111500
SUMMARY:Kid's Clubhouse: The Great Elephant Migration | Session I
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 30 spots left\nS
 tatus: futureSale\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/1988
 05\n\nCelebrate the arrival of The Great Elephant Migration in Boston with
  a hands-on family crafting experience inspired by one of the world's most
  meaningful public art initiatives.\n\nLed by children's book author Wendy
  Rouillard of Barnaby's Books & Toys\, young creators will build their own
  elephant habitats using a variety of nature-inspired materials. Each sess
 ion begins with a brief introduction to the story behind The Great Elephan
 t Migration\,introducing children to the importance of wildlife conservati
 on and the ways humans and animals can coexist.\n\nAfter crafting\, contin
 ue the adventure with brunch at Café Q\, where families can enjoy Journey
  to Kerala - a refreshing\, kid-friendly mocktail inspired by the elephant
 s' homeland\, featuring coconut water\, mango\, ginger\, lime\, curry leav
 es\, and sparkling club soda.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved
  for members\, plus their children aged 6+. Children may remain in the 'Ho
 use\, attended by a parent until 4:00PM. Please ensure you select the corr
 ect number of children's tickets when registering\, so we may account for 
 supplies. Adults do not require registration. If you have a larger family 
 (3+ kids) please email happening@thequin.com should you need an additional
  seat. As we anticipate a waitlist\, please be mindful of other families b
 y making any necessary cancellations at least 48-hours in advance.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/198805
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
